# Accepted Trivy findings.
#
# GO-2026-5932: golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained ("unsafe by design").
# SitHub imports ONLY golang.org/x/crypto/bcrypt (internal/users/store.go) for password
# hashing; the openpgp subpackage is never imported (verified: no `x/crypto/openpgp`
# import anywhere in the tree). No fixed version exists (deprecated package). Not applicable.
GO-2026-5932

# CVE-2026-93687 / GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm: braces stack-exhaustion DoS via deeply nested patterns.
# All braces versions are affected; no patched release exists yet. braces is a dev-only,
# lint-time dependency (@vue/eslint-config-typescript -> fast-glob -> micromatch -> braces)
# and is not part of the shipped frontend bundle. Remove once a fixed braces is released.
CVE-2026-93687
GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm

# GO-2026-6354 (CVE-2026-78662) / GO-2026-6355 (CVE-2026-56855): DoS on deadlocked channels in
# golang.org/x/crypto/ssh. SitHub imports ONLY golang.org/x/crypto/bcrypt; the ssh subpackage is
# never imported. The fix (x/crypto v0.56.0) requires Go 1.26 while SitHub targets Go 1.25.
# Remove once SitHub moves to Go 1.26 and x/crypto >= v0.56.0.
GO-2026-6354
CVE-2026-78662
GO-2026-6355
CVE-2026-56855
